# Prettier is scoped to first-party engine/tooling source via the format scripts
# (src bin scripts agents tests blind-tester ui). These globs are a belt-and-suspenders
# guard so an accidental `prettier .` never rewrites hash-sensitive or generated assets.
#
# Nothing first-party belongs here. A bare `ui` sat in this list from the original
# lint wiring and survived the cycle that added ui/ to the format scripts, so the gate
# matched zero files and reported success — the exclusion won, silently, for two months.
# dist/node_modules/coverage below are slash-free, so they already match ui/dist,
# ui/node_modules and ui/coverage at any depth; ui/ needs no entry of its own.
dist
node_modules
coverage
saves
ai-runs
.codex
# content YAML packs are content-hash-pinned — never reformat.
content
# trace fixtures carry committed hashes / known-answer vectors.
traces
# The Spark player prompt is deliberately compact and byte-contract tested;
# auto-formatting its JSON example spends model input without changing meaning.
blind-tester/prompt-overworld-spark.md
# tests/ is under the Prettier gate (bug_0036) EXCEPT the verification assets the
# integrity guard (scripts/verify-integrity.ts) freezes: the determinism property
# tests and the hash-pin/known-answer unit tests. A formatter must not churn a
# byte-frozen verifier asset (it reads as silent tampering to the drift gate), so
# these stay excluded — ESLint still lints them; only auto-formatting is held off.
tests/property/determinism.test.ts
tests/unit/rpg_validator.test.ts
tests/unit/sha256.test.ts
